    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "@albanD Using `.detach()` can also reproduce this issue, while `x.view(x.shape)` seems to resolve it. \nI think the underlying mechanism might be that:\n\nif an autograd function returns a view tensor, subsequent operations performed in a `no_grad` context / `autograd.Function.forward` will inherit the `requires_grad` attribute from the original tensor. \n\nThis can lead to unexpected behavior during gradient propagation.",
