    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "> Why would you expect `e` to require gradients here given that it was created in no_grad mode? \n\nThe examples are extracted from real use case, where they actually occur within autograd.Function rather than under torch.no_grad. In this implementation, the decision to retain activations relies on the requires_grad propagation introduced by the view operation in no_grad mode.\n\n",
